Andy has called Nellie into his office and this scene is really going to make the original title of this episode make sense because there's going to be a lot of workplace bullying.

1198
00:54:26.050 --> 00:54:26.310
Yeah.

1199
00:54:26.530 --> 00:54:30.730
He says he doesn't like to throw around the B word, but he's going to be a huge bitch to her.

1200
00:54:31.450 --> 00:54:31.910
Yeah.

1201
00:54:32.330 --> 00:54:33.150
God, Andy.

1202
00:54:33.150 --> 00:54:33.930
I know.

1203
00:54:34.130 --> 00:54:35.510
He doesn't stop there.

1204
00:54:35.670 --> 00:54:43.450
He's now set up in the parking lot a slack line to teach focus and discipline and in some cases humiliation.

1205
00:54:43.930 --> 00:54:44.250
Yeah.

1206
00:54:44.690 --> 00:54:51.170
He's gathered everyone down in the parking lot and he says, we're going to walk across it.

1207
00:54:51.310 --> 00:54:53.350
And if you make it, you're going to feel awesome.

1208
00:54:53.510 --> 00:54:56.030
But if you Toby out, you're going to feel like a real Nellie.

1209
00:54:56.510 --> 00:54:56.750
Yeah.

1210
00:54:56.750 --> 00:55:03.550
He's also brought along a couple of the instructors from his Outward Bound trip, Rafe and Feather.

1211
00:55:03.770 --> 00:55:03.970
Yeah.

1212
00:55:04.410 --> 00:55:06.150
So this scene would have continued.

1213
00:55:06.470 --> 00:55:12.470
I was in the script looking up some descriptions of the stunts and I came across this little nugget.

1214
00:55:12.890 --> 00:55:19.050
You know, Andy is referring to these guys by their Outward Bound names and they are going to refer to Andy as Iceman.

1215
00:55:19.250 --> 00:55:19.550
Right.

1216
00:55:19.550 --> 00:55:27.530
And then Rafe is going to explain to camera, we called him Iceman because he always complained about his canteen water being warm.

1217
00:55:28.390 --> 00:55:30.130
That's how Andy got his nickname.

1218
00:55:30.310 --> 00:55:36.230
Not because he was like really tough and could be out there freezing and be fine.

1219
00:55:36.990 --> 00:55:43.170
While Rafe and Feather are helping set up, Jem is going to find out that he has nothing in common with Plop.

1220
00:55:43.510 --> 00:55:43.970
Yeah.

1221
00:55:44.070 --> 00:55:46.730
He really tries to bond with him, but there's nothing.

1222
00:55:46.890 --> 00:55:48.990
He lists a bunch of things and there's nothing.

1223
00:55:48.990 --> 00:55:49.410
Nope.

1224
00:55:49.950 --> 00:55:51.730
We had a fan question from David H.

1225
00:55:51.830 --> 00:55:55.810
in Preston, England, who wanted to know who plays Feather, the tightrope guy.

1226
00:55:55.910 --> 00:55:57.470
He's not listed on IMDb.

1227
00:55:58.050 --> 00:56:01.750
Well, David, it was Cody Gilbert and he is a professional stunt person.

1228
00:56:02.230 --> 00:56:04.810
The character of Rafe was played by Jeff B.

1229
00:56:05.430 --> 00:56:08.410
First up on the slack line, Andy's going to make Nellie go.

1230
00:56:08.670 --> 00:56:10.730
He says, take off your heels, get up there.

1231
00:56:11.130 --> 00:56:12.990
She says, no, I'd rather keep them on.

1232
00:56:13.090 --> 00:56:14.590
I'm very insecure about my feet.

1233
00:56:14.590 --> 00:56:14.640
Right.

1234
00:56:15.270 --> 00:56:18.450
So she gets up on the slack line in high heels.

1235
00:56:18.730 --> 00:56:19.050
Yeah.

1236
00:56:19.350 --> 00:56:24.390
And we don't even know if she can do it because Andy immediately pushes her off face down.

1237
00:56:24.650 --> 00:56:25.130
Yes.

1238
00:56:25.470 --> 00:56:28.310
So we had a stunt person for Catherine Tate.

1239
00:56:28.850 --> 00:56:31.130
Catherine's stunt person was Jennifer Cobb.

1240
00:56:31.130 --> 00:56:36.770
But Catherine still had to try and get up on that slack line with the high heels.

1241
00:56:37.030 --> 00:56:42.090
Before we cut to the fall, that was really her in high heels getting up on that slack line.

1242
00:56:42.210 --> 00:56:42.910
It was bonkers.

1243
00:56:42.910 --> 00:56:48.450
I can't believe that you can just shove someone to the ground at work and not have any repercussions.

1244
00:56:48.830 --> 00:56:51.070
I mean, don't get me started.

1245
00:56:51.310 --> 00:56:51.750
Don't get me started.

1246
00:56:51.850 --> 00:56:57.190
There's a little something in the shooting draft I'm going to share here in a minute where they would have tried to address it.

1247
00:56:57.550 --> 00:56:59.210
Clark is now going to volunteer.

1248
00:56:59.670 --> 00:57:01.950
He gives it a try and he crushes it.

1249
00:57:02.370 --> 00:57:02.570
Yep.

1250
00:57:02.890 --> 00:57:04.830
This is going to inspire Dwight to try.

1251
00:57:05.070 --> 00:57:05.870
I mean, Dwight Jr.

1252
00:57:06.050 --> 00:57:06.330
did it.

1253
00:57:06.490 --> 00:57:07.370
Let's see Dwight Sr.

1254
00:57:07.590 --> 00:57:07.930
do it.

1255
00:57:08.110 --> 00:57:08.410
Yeah.

1256
00:57:09.130 --> 00:57:10.210
It doesn't go well.

1257
00:57:10.210 --> 00:57:14.610
How many times could one person fall off a slack line?

1258
00:57:14.830 --> 00:57:20.970
There was one time when he falls on his shoulder and I could barely watch it because it reminded me of breaking my own shoulder.

1259
00:57:21.410 --> 00:57:23.710
We had fan questions from Ashley O.

1260
00:57:23.870 --> 00:57:25.070
in Utah and Heather F.

1261
00:57:25.150 --> 00:57:29.050
in California who wanted to know, did Rain perform his own stunts?

1262
00:57:29.650 --> 00:57:32.990
Was it choreographed or planned how he would fall?

1263
00:57:33.570 --> 00:57:37.590
Did Rain make any of the creative decisions on how he would fall?

1264
00:57:37.590 --> 00:57:47.210
Well, I'll tell you guys, it was Rain and it was also his stunt double, Kevin Foster, who is also the person who doubles for him later on the bicycle.

1265
00:57:47.470 --> 00:57:48.330
We'll get to it.

1266
00:57:48.890 --> 00:57:55.370
But the descriptions for how he falls were meticulously scripted and I have them here to read to you.

1267
00:57:55.830 --> 00:58:03.450
First up, Dwight tries to step onto the slack line and is immediately pitched forward into a somersault and onto the mat.

1268
00:58:03.710 --> 00:58:04.970
We saw that move.

1269
00:58:05.630 --> 00:58:10.730
Next up, Dwight leaps onto the slack line again and is flung off even more violently.

1270
00:58:11.070 --> 00:58:13.750
He crawls around looking for his glasses and one of his shoes.

1271
00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:17.670
Next, Dwight keeps trying and gets flung off each time.

1272
00:58:18.210 --> 00:58:20.510
Ad-lib trash talking from Clark.

1273
00:58:21.230 --> 00:58:22.810
That was the note in the script.

1274
00:58:23.410 --> 00:58:26.090
Finally, it says Dwight has a bloody lip.

1275
00:58:26.310 --> 00:58:28.070
Nobody understands what he's saying.

1276
00:58:28.290 --> 00:58:31.310
Dwight becomes frustrated and runs off saying,

1277
00:58:31.310 --> 00:58:33.070
Buck you, brother buckers.

1278
00:58:34.270 --> 00:58:37.410
I did love that he tried the door and it wouldn't open.

1279
00:58:37.530 --> 00:58:37.930
Me too.

1280
00:58:37.970 --> 00:58:43.430
Because I feel like that's so classic when you want to quickly get away from a situation and you can't.

1281
00:58:43.650 --> 00:58:43.970
Yes.

1282
00:58:44.790 --> 00:58:52.230
Well, immediately after the slack line scene, Toby would have called a conference room meeting about workplace bullying.

1283
00:58:52.350 --> 00:58:54.090
It was in the shooting draft.

1284
00:58:54.090 --> 00:58:55.990
It's a really long conference room scene.

1285
00:58:56.190 --> 00:59:00.490
Everyone attends and they all share when they felt bullied by Andy.

1286
00:59:01.050 --> 00:59:02.930
I remember shooting this.

1287
00:59:03.150 --> 00:59:05.510
Jenna, they are some really hilarious moments.

1288
00:59:05.510 --> 00:59:08.230
I'm telling you right now, you and I broke a few times.

1289
00:59:08.690 --> 00:59:10.350
It's in the DVD extras.

1290
00:59:10.810 --> 00:59:13.430
I want to just share a few beats of it, okay?

1291
00:59:13.710 --> 00:59:13.930
Okay.

1292
00:59:14.510 --> 00:59:15.950
Toby starts off the meeting and says,

1293
00:59:15.950 --> 00:59:19.330
I felt bullied when Andy said he knew why Michael hated me.

1294
00:59:19.630 --> 00:59:20.410
Pete says,

1295
00:59:21.050 --> 00:59:24.610
I felt bullied by Andy when he gave me a nickname I'm not comfortable with.

1296
00:59:24.890 --> 00:59:26.150
And then Andy says,

1297
00:59:26.630 --> 00:59:28.050
Hey, Andy's a nickname.

1298
00:59:28.290 --> 00:59:30.330
Maybe you're bullying me right now.

1299
00:59:30.470 --> 00:59:31.730
And Toby says,

1300
00:59:32.250 --> 00:59:33.410
Toby's a nickname too.

1301
00:59:33.610 --> 00:59:34.870
It's short for Tobert.

1302
00:59:35.270 --> 00:59:35.730
Wow.

1303
00:59:36.010 --> 00:59:37.430
You're changing the subject.

1304
00:59:38.050 --> 00:59:39.370
Then Kevin says,

1305
00:59:39.790 --> 00:59:40.870
Angela bullies me.

1306
00:59:41.110 --> 00:59:44.370
She won't let me have her cat because I killed my turtle so many times.

1307
00:59:45.030 --> 00:59:47.190
Everyone starts turning on everyone.

1308
00:59:47.470 --> 00:59:51.910
Then somehow everyone ends up ganging up on Creed and he leaves the room

1309
00:59:51.910 --> 00:59:56.710
and the camera follows him to that hallway where we all go to have private conversations

1310
00:59:56.710 --> 00:59:58.390
and Creed starts crying.

1311
00:59:58.630 --> 00:59:59.230
Oh no.

1312
00:59:59.530 --> 00:59:59.870
Yeah.

1313
01:00:00.390 --> 01:00:05.430
Then it comes back to the conference room scene and things get really heated between Phyllis and Angela.

1314
01:00:05.690 --> 01:00:06.530
You have to hear it.

1315
01:00:07.030 --> 01:00:08.190
And how can I be a bully?

1316
01:00:08.190 --> 01:00:09.210
I'm a sweetie pie.

1317
01:00:09.350 --> 01:00:10.570
You're a bitch.

1318
01:00:11.890 --> 01:00:12.770
Oh God.

1319
01:00:15.110 --> 01:00:16.610
Oh my gosh.

1320
01:00:18.890 --> 01:00:20.210
Calls Phyllis a bitch.

1321
01:00:20.390 --> 01:00:21.330
And then Stanley goes,

1322
01:00:21.510 --> 01:00:21.870
Oh no.

1323
01:00:22.130 --> 01:00:25.990
And Stanley has brought an extra crossword and passes it to Jim.

1324
01:00:26.530 --> 01:00:29.270
And then Jim leans over to Pam and goes,

1325
01:00:29.590 --> 01:00:31.450
Well, I guess I'm not even the new Jim.

1326
01:00:31.570 --> 01:00:32.730
Now I'm the new Stanley.

1327
01:00:33.190 --> 01:00:34.330
And then Pam goes,

1328
01:00:34.430 --> 01:00:36.550
Well, if you become the new Creed, I'll divorce you.

1329
01:00:36.550 --> 01:00:38.810
Right as Creed is coming back in.

1330
01:00:38.810 --> 01:00:41.550
And then he starts tearing up again.

1331
01:00:42.770 --> 01:00:43.510
Oh my gosh.

1332
01:00:43.690 --> 01:00:46.610
I am remembering this now as you describe it.

1333
01:00:46.690 --> 01:00:48.950
It was a huge epic conference room scene.

1334
01:00:49.650 --> 01:00:55.670
Well, instead, this episode goes to the warehouse where Dwight is deconstructing a bicycle.

1335
01:00:55.970 --> 01:01:00.470
I'll have you know that this was also meticulously described in the script.

1336
01:01:00.650 --> 01:01:04.490
There was a whole paragraph describing how he takes this bicycle apart.

1337
01:01:04.490 --> 01:01:08.090
And it just delighted me because it's very Greg Daniels.

1338
01:01:08.410 --> 01:01:17.990
I bet Greg literally met with so many people and they had to have precise like drawings and sketches and the physics of it and how it worked.

1339
01:01:18.170 --> 01:01:20.010
Angela, he made sketches.

1340
01:01:20.430 --> 01:01:21.230
I'm sure he did.

1341
01:01:21.230 --> 01:01:22.350
He just sent them to me.

1342
01:01:22.550 --> 01:01:27.090
When we get up on the roof, like the whole thing, he sketched it out.

1343
01:01:27.210 --> 01:01:32.010
And this is like, this is the mad scientist part of Greg's brain.

1344
01:01:32.410 --> 01:01:37.250
And I think Greg would think he could really do this stunt.

1345
01:01:37.830 --> 01:01:39.450
He just needs a counterweight.

1346
01:01:39.610 --> 01:01:40.170
That's all.

1347
01:01:40.410 --> 01:01:40.570
Sure.

1348
01:01:40.970 --> 01:01:43.810
Just grab a printer and duct tape it to the bottom of the bicycle.

1349
01:01:43.930 --> 01:01:44.410
No problem.

1350
01:01:44.630 --> 01:01:44.830
Yeah.

1351
01:01:44.830 --> 01:01:50.510
But first, first, I do believe that Greg would ask someone to sit on the bar.

1352
01:01:50.850 --> 01:01:51.770
I do.

1353
01:01:52.990 --> 01:01:54.630
We got ahead of ourselves.

1354
01:01:54.710 --> 01:01:59.910
As you know, Dwight is going to call Pam up onto the roof and reveal what he's doing in the warehouse.

1355
01:02:00.130 --> 01:02:06.850
And he explains that he is going to ride a bicycle, I guess, from the top of the building to a phone pole.

1356
01:02:07.150 --> 01:02:09.550
And he wants Pam to be his counterweight.

1357
01:02:09.550 --> 01:02:10.610
And she refuses.

1358
01:02:11.050 --> 01:02:12.130
It's a whole thing.

1359
01:02:12.130 --> 01:02:16.850
Well, I'll have you know on the call sheet for this day, we filmed on August 1st, which is a Wednesday.

1360
01:02:17.150 --> 01:02:21.330
And the comments on the call sheet were that temperatures were going to exceed 85 degrees.

1361
01:02:21.530 --> 01:02:22.450
Please stay hydrated.

1362
01:02:22.910 --> 01:02:24.490
Avoid the sun whenever possible.

1363
01:02:24.870 --> 01:02:28.150
See the safety bulletin posted by the medic for more information.

1364
01:02:28.450 --> 01:02:35.270
And that stunt rehearsals and tests for Thursday's aerial work would begin when the company moves to the alley mid-afternoon.

1365
01:02:35.490 --> 01:02:36.170
I see.

1366
01:02:36.450 --> 01:02:36.770
Yeah.

1367
01:02:37.190 --> 01:02:38.330
Stunt rehearsals.

1368
01:02:38.950 --> 01:02:40.550
This was a huge stunt.

1369
01:02:40.550 --> 01:02:50.810
Well, meanwhile, Angela is interviewing Pete, who doesn't want Comstock, yet is going through an extensive interview about his goals in life.

1370
01:02:50.990 --> 01:02:51.150
Yeah.

1371
01:02:51.270 --> 01:02:52.710
She says, why do you want this cat?

1372
01:02:52.930 --> 01:02:54.130
He says, I don't want it.

1373
01:02:54.330 --> 01:02:56.430
She says, how would you support the cat?

1374
01:02:56.590 --> 01:02:57.510
What are your ambitions?

1375
01:02:57.950 --> 01:02:59.770
Pete says, I want to start my own business.

1376
01:02:59.770 --> 01:03:01.030
I want to be a millionaire.

1377
01:03:01.250 --> 01:03:01.930
Lots of things.

1378
01:03:02.090 --> 01:03:02.410
Travel.

1379
01:03:02.630 --> 01:03:04.070
Make the world a better place.

1380
01:03:04.250 --> 01:03:05.550
Earn an MBA at night.

1381
01:03:05.550 --> 01:03:08.990
Angela says, have you taken any concrete steps?

1382
01:03:09.290 --> 01:03:15.210
He says, well, I'm still just fitting in here, you know, getting used to the new job, but definitely on the agenda.

1383
01:03:15.450 --> 01:03:16.810
It's a good idea, Angela.

1384
01:03:17.010 --> 01:03:17.970
I should make a liSt.

1385
01:03:19.010 --> 01:03:19.230
Oh.

1386
01:03:19.690 --> 01:03:21.490
Jim is listening to all of this.

1387
01:03:21.610 --> 01:03:22.730
It is hitting him hard.

1388
01:03:23.110 --> 01:03:26.350
He has a talking head immediately after where he says, you know what?

1389
01:03:26.350 --> 01:03:29.690
If he's not careful, he'll get stuck there for years doing nothing.

1390
01:03:30.490 --> 01:03:31.030
Wow.

1391
01:03:31.750 --> 01:03:34.110
Maybe Pete is the new Jim after all.

1392
01:03:34.530 --> 01:03:34.890
Mm-hmm.

1393
01:03:35.290 --> 01:03:41.470
Angela is now going to explain to Pete that the reason she's getting rid of Comstock is because the baby is allergic.

1394
01:03:42.130 --> 01:03:45.290
And that Comstock is the senator's favorite cat.

1395
01:03:45.490 --> 01:03:45.630
Yeah.

1396
01:03:45.630 --> 01:03:46.890
And he's heartbroken.

1397
01:03:47.130 --> 01:03:48.450
Heartbroken over this.

1398
01:03:48.690 --> 01:03:51.110
Oh, do Oscar's ears perk up.

1399
01:03:51.350 --> 01:03:52.650
He says, you know what?

1400
01:03:52.730 --> 01:03:53.670
I will take the cat.

1401
01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:55.550
Angela is overjoyed.

1402
01:03:55.550 --> 01:03:56.050
Mm-hmm.

1403
01:03:56.050 --> 01:03:57.650
She's like, thank you, Oscar.

1404
01:03:58.290 --> 01:03:58.690
Yeah.

1405
01:03:58.790 --> 01:04:01.230
Oscar says, I'll come pick him up this evening.

1406
01:04:01.230 --> 01:04:08.930
And Angela says, oh, boy, well, Robert won't get to say goodbye, I guess, because he told me he has plans tonight.

1407
01:04:09.450 --> 01:04:09.790
Yeah.

1408
01:04:10.110 --> 01:04:11.570
And Oscar says, c'est la vie.

1409
01:04:11.910 --> 01:04:15.410
And Angela says, please don't teach French to my cat.

1410
01:04:15.650 --> 01:04:16.010
Mm-hmm.

1411
01:04:16.310 --> 01:04:16.510
Yeah.

1412
01:04:16.950 --> 01:04:18.970
Well, then Oscar's going to sneak away.

1413
01:04:19.250 --> 01:04:20.390
He's on the phone.

1414
01:04:20.570 --> 01:04:21.970
And guess who he's talking to?

1415
01:04:22.230 --> 01:04:24.470
His date for the evening, Robert.

1416
01:04:24.890 --> 01:04:25.250
Yep.

1417
01:04:25.550 --> 01:04:29.510
He says, you're going to be able to play with Comstock tonight at dinner.

1418
01:04:29.910 --> 01:04:30.470
Mm-hmm.

1419
01:04:30.710 --> 01:04:31.650
I have a question.

1420
01:04:32.310 --> 01:04:34.810
How do we think Gerald is going to like Comstock?

1421
01:04:35.150 --> 01:04:35.890
I know.

1422
01:04:36.130 --> 01:04:38.910
There's a whole dog-cat introduction that needs to happen here.

1423
01:04:39.090 --> 01:04:39.430
Yeah.

1424
01:04:39.750 --> 01:04:41.970
Oscar must really like the senator.

1425
01:04:42.250 --> 01:04:43.150
A lot.

1426
01:04:43.390 --> 01:04:43.850
Mm-hmm.

1427
01:04:44.050 --> 01:04:45.950
Because he said he's a dog person.

1428
01:04:46.190 --> 01:04:46.450
Yeah.

1429
01:04:46.830 --> 01:04:49.470
Now it's the end of the day and everyone's leaving.

1430
01:04:49.870 --> 01:04:51.050
Jim is going to linger.

1431
01:04:51.050 --> 01:04:53.170
He says, I'll meet you down there, Pam.

1432
01:04:53.750 --> 01:04:55.390
I can barely talk about it.

1433
01:04:55.430 --> 01:04:56.570
It makes me so upset.

1434
01:04:57.330 --> 01:04:57.650
Well.

1435
01:04:58.510 --> 01:04:59.290
I know.

1436
01:04:59.410 --> 01:04:59.850
I know.

1437
01:05:00.010 --> 01:05:05.750
I have to say, though, I thought John's performance of Jim in this moment was so great.

1438
01:05:05.950 --> 01:05:06.430
So good.

1439
01:05:06.430 --> 01:05:09.330
You can see how torn up inside he is about it.

1440
01:05:09.470 --> 01:05:12.090
He goes to call his friend.

1441
01:05:12.450 --> 01:05:14.170
Then he bails.

1442
01:05:14.370 --> 01:05:15.230
He's like, no, no.

1443
01:05:15.350 --> 01:05:15.970
And he gets up.

1444
01:05:16.070 --> 01:05:17.750
And then he goes back and he does it.

1445
01:05:18.250 --> 01:05:22.790
And when he finally commits and says, I'm all in and hangs up, he's like, yes.

1446
01:05:23.290 --> 01:05:25.430
It felt so good for him.

1447
01:05:26.370 --> 01:05:27.150
It's hard.

1448
01:05:27.290 --> 01:05:27.630
It's hard.

1449
01:05:27.750 --> 01:05:32.910
I feel, you know, obviously, like as someone in a relationship, I'm like, hey, what are

1450
01:05:32.910 --> 01:05:33.290
you doing?

1451
01:05:33.570 --> 01:05:35.890
You got to include your partner in this moment.

1452
01:05:36.050 --> 01:05:36.830
What are you doing?

1453
01:05:37.190 --> 01:05:41.350
And then at the same time, I see how much he's struggling with making this decision.

1454
01:05:41.730 --> 01:05:43.570
I thought it was played out really well.

1455
01:05:43.790 --> 01:05:47.610
Well, the whole point of the storyline is to create tension in this relationship.

1456
01:05:47.750 --> 01:05:47.930
Yeah.

1457
01:05:47.930 --> 01:05:49.570
And this is going to do it.

1458
01:05:49.690 --> 01:05:52.010
I wrote in all caps, this is not right.

1459
01:05:52.390 --> 01:05:53.630
Talk to your wife firSt.

1460
01:05:53.970 --> 01:05:57.650
This is a major life decision that affects the entire family.

1461
01:05:58.350 --> 01:06:05.230
And when we were talking about this over the summer, I said, this would devastate me.

1462
01:06:05.370 --> 01:06:11.430
It would devastate me if my husband and I sat down, we talked about a life decision, we made

1463
01:06:11.430 --> 01:06:17.670
an agreement, and then without talking to me first, he changed that agreement and took

1464
01:06:17.670 --> 01:06:18.450
some action.

1465
01:06:18.790 --> 01:06:24.230
It would devastate me not because he took the action, but because he felt like he couldn't

1466
01:06:24.230 --> 01:06:28.870
trust me enough to talk about it a second time.

1467
01:06:29.150 --> 01:06:30.250
Well, that's the big thing.

1468
01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:37.050
That's it right there, which is when you're in a partnership, a partnership is sharing.

1469
01:06:38.050 --> 01:06:44.810
And the fact that Jim didn't feel like he could share this with his partner, that's

1470
01:06:44.810 --> 01:06:46.910
the real thing when you peel back the layers.

1471
01:06:47.170 --> 01:06:47.270
Yeah.

1472
01:06:47.430 --> 01:06:50.610
Why couldn't he share this with Pam?

1473
01:06:51.070 --> 01:06:51.390
Yes.

1474
01:06:51.590 --> 01:06:54.650
And that would eat away at me as his partner.

1475
01:06:54.890 --> 01:06:56.870
It would eat away at me to think about.

1476
01:06:57.110 --> 01:07:00.650
Well, then your mind jumps to, well, what else do you not feel comfortable sharing with

1477
01:07:00.650 --> 01:07:00.830
me?

1478
01:07:00.830 --> 01:07:01.470
Exactly.

1479
01:07:01.850 --> 01:07:08.850
Because I truly believe, as Pam, that if Jim came to me and said, I've been thinking

1480
01:07:08.850 --> 01:07:15.850
about this, and I have to say, I want to do it, and I know it's going to be crazy, and

1481
01:07:15.850 --> 01:07:17.130
I know it means Philadelphia.

1482
01:07:17.130 --> 01:07:18.990
Can we make this work for me?

1483
01:07:19.110 --> 01:07:21.590
That Pam would have said, yes.

1484
01:07:21.990 --> 01:07:25.350
But he didn't give her the opportunity to support him.

1485
01:07:25.350 --> 01:07:30.610
He went off on his own, and he made a decision, and as we're going to find out in the next

1486
01:07:30.610 --> 01:07:35.210
episode, keeps that decision from her for a long time.

1487
01:07:35.330 --> 01:07:40.470
He does not go home tonight and say anything to her for weeks.

1488
01:07:40.690 --> 01:07:42.330
That's another layer to it.

1489
01:07:42.390 --> 01:07:43.770
That's the betrayal to me.

1490
01:07:44.010 --> 01:07:44.270
Yeah.

1491
01:07:44.470 --> 01:07:48.470
And, you know, he sort of alludes to the fact that he didn't want to tell her until it was

1492
01:07:48.470 --> 01:07:48.850
real.

1493
01:07:49.510 --> 01:07:52.430
But the minute he said, I'm all in, it was real.

1494
01:07:52.770 --> 01:07:53.230
Yes.

1495
01:07:53.230 --> 01:07:57.310
And it has the potential to uproot their life in a major way.

1496
01:07:57.550 --> 01:07:57.690
Yeah.

1497
01:07:58.090 --> 01:07:58.590
Ah.

1498
01:07:59.570 --> 01:08:03.130
It just, I see the foreshadowing of what is to come.

1499
01:08:03.470 --> 01:08:08.390
I thought it was brilliantly acted and written because it's doing everything it was supposed

1500
01:08:08.390 --> 01:08:08.830
to do.

1501
01:08:08.990 --> 01:08:09.310
Yes.

1502
01:08:09.670 --> 01:08:12.010
Well, we're now in the parking lot.

1503
01:08:12.730 --> 01:08:15.750
Dwight has found a counterweight for his bicycle.

1504
01:08:16.030 --> 01:08:16.370
Mm-hmm.

1505
01:08:16.610 --> 01:08:18.390
He calls down to his co-workers.

1506
01:08:18.410 --> 01:08:22.970
He says he's going to show the cool new guys what a real salesman looks like.

1507
01:08:23.230 --> 01:08:25.630
You only live once and he's going to prove it.

1508
01:08:26.010 --> 01:08:30.030
Lady, I want you to know in the call sheet for the shoot day, there were an additional

1509
01:08:30.030 --> 01:08:32.890
five pages of safety bulletins.

1510
01:08:33.990 --> 01:08:34.950
Five pages.

1511
01:08:35.230 --> 01:08:35.830
I believe it.

1512
01:08:35.970 --> 01:08:38.570
Of all the different precautions they were taking.

1513
01:08:39.050 --> 01:08:42.070
Well, Dwight is going to ride the bike along the wire.

1514
01:08:42.070 --> 01:08:45.790
But when he gets midway, it tips over.

1515
01:08:45.790 --> 01:08:50.790
He is dangling from the handlebars and has to be rescued by the fire department.

1516
01:08:51.170 --> 01:08:53.590
We got a fan question from Juan R.

1517
01:08:53.770 --> 01:08:55.170
in Duluth, Georgia, who said,

1518
01:08:55.450 --> 01:08:59.530
Tell us everything about Rain's cycling stunt in this episode.

1519
01:08:59.730 --> 01:09:00.590
Well, of course.

1520
01:09:00.830 --> 01:09:02.490
I reached out to Steve Burgess.

1521
01:09:02.650 --> 01:09:03.450
He's the beSt.

1522
01:09:03.450 --> 01:09:07.510
And he said, Oh, there's a lot to say about this stunt.

1523
01:09:07.890 --> 01:09:12.290
He said they started with the rough concept drawings that Greg did.

1524
01:09:12.490 --> 01:09:15.390
Greg drew it all out, how he imagined it in his head.

1525
01:09:15.590 --> 01:09:20.870
They brought in Al and Brent Jones, the stunt coordinators, and started discussing how to

1526
01:09:20.870 --> 01:09:21.670
make it a reality.

1527
01:09:22.150 --> 01:09:24.930
They brought in Pat Romano to do all the rigging.

1528
01:09:25.590 --> 01:09:28.230
Steve said we had to put in our own telephone pole.

1529
01:09:28.370 --> 01:09:31.750
We could not use the real one for safety and legal reasons.

1530
01:09:31.750 --> 01:09:32.490
Well, yeah.

1531
01:09:32.810 --> 01:09:35.810
So we had to put a second telephone pole up.

1532
01:09:35.990 --> 01:09:39.090
Let's not tie this to something that has electricity.

1533
01:09:39.470 --> 01:09:40.030
That's right.

1534
01:09:40.270 --> 01:09:45.150
We also had to put the giant crane that you mentioned in the parking lot in order to get

1535
01:09:45.150 --> 01:09:47.010
the wire across the roof.

1536
01:09:47.230 --> 01:09:54.570
He said that the ends of the wire were attached to huge grade walls, which are like bulldozers,

1537
01:09:55.230 --> 01:09:58.710
because that would really keep it strong, right?

1538
01:09:58.710 --> 01:10:02.010
He said it took over a week just to do all the rigging.

1539
01:10:02.170 --> 01:10:05.630
And for the stunt, they had a giant airbag in the parking lot.

1540
01:10:05.750 --> 01:10:07.370
And I remember it.

1541
01:10:07.470 --> 01:10:08.590
I remember it, too.

1542
01:10:08.810 --> 01:10:10.450
It's also in the call sheet.

1543
01:10:10.630 --> 01:10:14.750
There were multiple pages just describing this airbag.

1544
01:10:14.930 --> 01:10:16.070
Steve sent us pictures.

1545
01:10:16.370 --> 01:10:17.350
We'll put it in stories.

1546
01:10:17.810 --> 01:10:20.590
Steve also mentioned that it was really windy that day.

1547
01:10:20.750 --> 01:10:21.290
Oh, Lord.

1548
01:10:21.290 --> 01:10:25.630
And it was actually hard to ride the bike on the wire because of the wind.

1549
01:10:25.930 --> 01:10:30.650
And so he said we did three takes of the stunt, but it worked.

1550
01:10:30.770 --> 01:10:34.470
I remember standing in the parking lot looking up at the stunt guy.

1551
01:10:34.590 --> 01:10:35.510
All of us there.

1552
01:10:35.750 --> 01:10:39.150
I was convinced I was going to see a death that day.

1553
01:10:39.270 --> 01:10:40.150
I'm going to be honest with you.

1554
01:10:40.250 --> 01:10:41.490
I was terrified.

1555
01:10:41.670 --> 01:10:44.710
It was the most stressful thing.

1556
01:10:44.710 --> 01:10:52.810
I don't know how anyone works on action movies where they do all of these crazy stunts.

1557
01:10:52.950 --> 01:10:54.450
It was so terrifying.

1558
01:10:54.690 --> 01:10:55.650
So terrifying.

1559
01:10:56.290 --> 01:11:00.770
Steve Burgess says the shot of rain hanging from the bike is actually rain.

1560
01:11:01.270 --> 01:11:05.990
However, what they did was they built a scaffold under the bike.

1561
01:11:06.190 --> 01:11:10.570
So rain was actually just about eight or 10 inches above the scaffold.

1562
01:11:10.870 --> 01:11:11.810
I remember that, too.

1563
01:11:11.950 --> 01:11:13.130
And that was still scary.

1564
01:11:13.130 --> 01:11:15.150
I have photos of that as well.

1565
01:11:16.210 --> 01:11:21.770
We also had to hire a stunt fireman to carry Rain's stunt double down the firetruck ladder.

1566
01:11:22.330 --> 01:11:26.610
It is not easy to carry someone down a ladder like that.

1567
01:11:26.810 --> 01:11:31.290
It was described in the shooting draft that the fireman carried Dwight down like a bride.

1568
01:11:32.730 --> 01:11:34.370
I like that description.

1569
01:11:35.170 --> 01:11:41.550
And Steve Burgess said there were many, many, many safety meetings about this.

1570
01:11:41.550 --> 01:11:45.450
And it even had to include the NBC safety guy.

1571
01:11:45.710 --> 01:11:49.350
There were a lot of people who had to sign off on this stunt before we did it.

1572
01:11:49.650 --> 01:11:54.350
Well, this episode is going to end with Nellie at her desk.

1573
01:11:54.390 --> 01:11:58.490
She is surrounded by big recycling bins.

1574
01:11:58.790 --> 01:12:02.770
And people are tossing their trash towards her.

1575
01:12:03.110 --> 01:12:05.530
She's getting hit by the trash.

1576
01:12:06.370 --> 01:12:07.830
I hated this.

1577
01:12:07.970 --> 01:12:08.790
I didn't buy it.

1578
01:12:08.970 --> 01:12:11.190
I didn't think that other people would participate.

1579
01:12:11.390 --> 01:12:11.690
Same!

1580
01:12:11.850 --> 01:12:14.070
I didn't think that Phyllis or Stanley would do this.

1581
01:12:14.250 --> 01:12:14.490
Agree.

1582
01:12:14.670 --> 01:12:16.530
We get that Andy has a beef with her.

1583
01:12:16.830 --> 01:12:18.530
I don't think anyone else cares.

1584
01:12:18.910 --> 01:12:19.810
I'm with you.

1585
01:12:20.390 --> 01:12:23.950
Andy says he's passionate about two things, recycling and revenge.

1586
01:12:24.330 --> 01:12:29.330
Now Nellie's in the conference room doing a talking head, but there's still trash coming at her.

1587
01:12:30.030 --> 01:12:32.210
She's trying to be positive.

1588
01:12:32.410 --> 01:12:33.410
She goes, that's a fluke.

1589
01:12:34.270 --> 01:12:36.790
Well, I don't think we should end on that note.

1590
01:12:36.970 --> 01:12:43.450
Let's end on an upbeat note, which is one last get-to-know-your-cast-and-crew from the call sheet.

1591
01:12:43.450 --> 01:12:43.950
My new favorite segment.

1592
01:12:44.190 --> 01:12:48.070
This one is about Joseph, who was part of our security team.

1593
01:12:48.190 --> 01:12:49.510
Oh, I remember Joseph.

1594
01:12:49.670 --> 01:12:50.090
Yes.

1595
01:12:50.290 --> 01:12:52.670
Things you did not know about Joseph Wang.

1596
01:12:52.990 --> 01:12:56.190
Joseph knows Chinese, Taiwanese, and English.

1597
01:12:56.190 --> 01:12:58.950
His favorite books are the Harry Potter books.

1598
01:12:59.190 --> 01:13:02.270
The prettiest place he has ever been is Paris.

1599
01:13:02.690 --> 01:13:05.750
His favorite superhero is Speedy Gonzales.

1600
01:13:06.230 --> 01:13:10.890
His first encounter with the TV film business was security, of course.

1601
01:13:11.190 --> 01:13:15.470
And he was once a sports agent and has three tattoos.

1602
01:13:15.810 --> 01:13:16.870
I love this.

1603
01:13:17.010 --> 01:13:21.270
And we ran into Joseph because he now does security for The Kelly Clarkson Show.

1604
01:13:21.450 --> 01:13:22.390
We were so excited.

1605
01:13:22.390 --> 01:13:23.230
We took pictures.

1606
01:13:23.410 --> 01:13:24.030
We hugged.

1607
01:13:24.150 --> 01:13:25.530
Office family forever.

1608
01:13:25.530 --> 01:13:28.390
Aw, well, guys, that was new, guys.

1609
01:13:28.850 --> 01:13:34.430
A big thank you to Greg Daniels and to Steve Burgess for your contributions to this episode.

1610
01:13:35.170 --> 01:13:37.090
I think we're off to a good start.

1611
01:13:37.090 --> 01:13:38.710
I'm excited for this season.

1612
01:13:38.870 --> 01:13:40.890
Next up is Roy's wedding.

1613
01:13:41.570 --> 01:13:42.410
Chore wheel.

1614
01:13:42.890 --> 01:13:43.810
Chore wheel.

1615
01:13:44.070 --> 01:13:46.770
And I'm sorry, Roy plays the piano now?

1616
01:13:46.950 --> 01:13:47.330
Oh.

1617
01:13:47.470 --> 01:13:48.190
Excuse me?

1618
01:13:48.210 --> 01:13:49.310
It's so delicious.

1619
01:13:50.110 --> 01:13:51.270
See you next week.

1620
